Room: an extension-origin device chooser looks up the toolbar through the
registered ToolbarButtonProvider (null-safe) instead of the BrowserView, so a
Room Browser (no BrowserView; RoomToolbarButtonProvider returns no extensions
container) rejects the chooser safely instead of dereferencing a missing view.

Rebased 3.8 (154.0.8037.58 -> 154.0.8037.98): upstream's fullscreen-drop
hardening (92300d69b6811, "Harden the device chooser dialog against fullscreen
drops") moved the lookup after a new DropFullscreenForChooserDialog() and added
its own `if (!browser_view) return base::DoNothing();`. The hook moved with the
call site: the provider lookup replaces both the BrowserView lookup and that
null check (the provider is null-checked in its place). With upstream's check a
Room Browser is already rejected without this patch; whether 0012 can be
dropped is the planner's call (B-61).

